<p>The Pentagon says three U.S. service members were killed and five others were seriously wounded during U.S. operations tied to the ongoing U.S.-Israeli campaign against Iran. They are the first confirmed American combat deaths since the strikes began over the weekend. U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) said several additional troops suffered minor shrapnel injuries and concussions and are being returned to duty. The deaths come as Iran carries out retaliatory attacks across the Middle East and the wider conflict continues to escalate. CBS News reported that the U.S. casualties were among American personnel based in Kuwait.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/iV3HStrjymCCvFl3WYo_WEmJDUJqZ_wa9VldNG7f1wnURjJbi_WBZAOtdEkhJtBQcTDEuoOW3jelUmUdozNWw0j1RFBstDcyiiCAYZID-i6SnpQ2jWeZDW5rcyq5lD98540g9EF_4VkIsXfYjDD08Nkt37HaKj-fTBcMDdn1EfFw8GVGDDQrI8iE-g9tezxdqxBMMd7j8fHxQR8aWYy2eEJLUwE' alt='President Trump on Friday; he warned the campaign could bring U.S. deaths.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Disclosure limits: CENTCOM announced the deaths in a public post but did not say when or where they occurred.</li><li>Retaliation context: Time reported the Pentagon’s announcement followed Iranian retaliatory missile strikes aimed at U.S. bases across the Middle East.</li><li>Leadership aim: President Trump said the strikes were intended to bring about a change in Iran’s leadership, according to Time.</li></ul><blockquote>Major combat operations continue and our response effort is ongoing - U.S. Central Command</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM): CENTCOM said the response effort is ongoing and described the situation as fluid. In its public statement, it did not specify when or where the troops were killed. (<a href='https://time.com/7381938/us-soldiers-killed-iran/'>Time</a>, <a href='https://www.boston.com/news/politics/2026/03/01/3-us-troops-killed-and-5-are-seriously-wounded-during-iran-attacks-military-says/'>Boston.com</a>, <a href='h